"README.md":"""# StudyMate starter app
A mobile-first student app built with HTML/CSS/JavaScript. Assignments and notes are saved in your browser/device using localStorage. It works offline after first load when hosted; this starter can be wrapped into an Android APK.

## Phone-only path to APK
1. Upload these files to a GitHub repository (create a repository named `studymate`).
2. To make a web preview, enable GitHub Pages: Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch → `main` → `/ (root)`.
3. For an APK, use a Capacitor Android wrapper and GitHub Actions build workflow. This needs Android SDK/Gradle in the GitHub runner; you do not need to install them on your phone.
4. Install only APKs you built or trust. Android may ask permission to install from your browser/files app.

## Current starter features
- Assignment creation, completion and deletion
- Notes create/edit/delete and search
- Reading mode with font controls
- Dark mode
- Local storage
"""
